# The restart of an agent whose queued saves left an alarm's last_transition_id on an older entry (`order`): the
# pointer of an alarm that had no later insert names its unlink's REMOVED entry, so no REMOVED row is injected for
# it, that old entry is what the load brings back, and the alarm's event ids start again from it.
database real
rules tests/corpus/sql/save.conf
queue 1
chart loop.s loop.s_name loop.sql disks things 1
label loop.s kind ssd
var loop.s v 10
pending host-recheck
pending chart-recheck loop.s
clock 0
pass 0
clock 1
store
clock 2
pass 2
clock 3
store
clock 100
restart
clock 101
pass 101
clock 102
store
clock 103
pass 103
clock 104
alarm-log 0
